bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/
node_modules/

# ~/.gitignore_global line 3 ignores .mcp.json everywhere - a sensible default for ordinary repos,
# and exactly wrong here, where .mcp.json IS the deliverable. A repo .gitignore takes precedence
# over core.excludesFile, so this negation un-ignores it structurally.
#
# Committing it via `git add -f` would also work and would rot: the next person (or the next me)
# commits normally, .mcp.json silently stays out, the plugin installs and serves NOTHING, and the
# failure looks like a broken server rather than a missing file. Never `git add -f -A` either -
# that overrides .gitignore wholesale and drags in node_modules.
!.mcp.json

# The published server is committed - the plugin is served from this path, not built on the fly.
!bundle/
